cause a lot of  times if you forget to charge your  laptop you don't use it for a couple  days if you're a light user you pick it  up and it's dead you need to go  somewhere well you're dealing with an  issue now it is great and on top of that  you can fast charge it from a usb type-c  power bank as well that you can buy  inexpensively which is awesome i'll  leave a link down below and i've already  benefited from having those two  thunderbolt ports available even when  you're charging thanks to the max 8  connection which now has stronger  magnets than before and it comes with  beautiful color matched braided cables  and that just proves one of my big  points that this is a luxury  item it is beautiful the design is great  it looks modern and sleek with those  slim even bezels the cable the  presentation everything just screams  luxury as does the price point now the  webcam fantastic speakers definitely  better than any laptop this size the m1  macbook air the previous version we  actually do like those speakers better  they are louder have a little bit more  highs this has a little bit more bass it  wasn't that big of a jump but it still  sounds great and if you're watching  music movies anything you're going to be  happy now as far as performance it is  dang good as well  at least if you have the higher spec  model and you're doing shorter bursty  loads now i spent time comparing both of  these systems we have a full detailed  comparison available i use them at home  for some video editing for some photo  editing and they do a good job  especially compared to what the intel  macbook airs were capable of just a few  years ago  you can now not only edit 4k video and  final cut you can even edit 8k  hevc compressed video that almost nobody  is shooting now sure if you're going to  be working with stuff like raw footage  or heavier things that is where you  would want to upgrade to the 14-inch  when we tested that in the pro it fell  apart and the 14-inch handle it great  which is why we recommended that model  but if you're somebody that wants to do  youtube you want to maybe edit even tik  tok videos with more effects on your  computer you want to do photos this will  handle it very well the big issue and  the first sad issue is the divide  between the base model and then what you  get if you spend 400 more  never have we seen  such a big performance gap between the  same machine with the same chip and even  the same graphics as we have with these  apple silicon chips and the  configurations that apple offers for  example with a 2020 macbook air you  could upgrade to an i7 spend 300 bucks  more but the difference wouldn't be that  big same thing with upgrading graphics  but when have we seen  basically a doubling of speed by just  upgrading to a higher ssd and an extra  eight gigs of ram and that is with  having no program opened other than  lightroom and if you do some simple  multitasking like everybody does having  email open google drive a youtube video  the difference is  shocking a difference like this should  not exist and the same thing goes for  video editing apple put in prores  decoders and encoders into the m2 chip  which we did not expect but then if you  get the base model those ships are  worthless because of how slow the system  gets with the base model now i don't  want to keep hammering on about this  because most people that care know about  it already and people are switching  they're buying configurations  drastically which means that we did get  the word out there just know that if you  buy the base model it is even slower  than the m1 macbook air in a lot of real  world scenarios which is very sad now we  also covered the thermal capabilities  and limitations with this system and the  sad part about that is it's not that  apple didn't put in a fan or were  pushing it too hard is that the m1 had a  way better cooler than the m2 they  actually had a thick heat sink that  transfers heat and spreads it whereas  now it's a thin almost foil-like  material that is sealed in with this  layer that keeps heat in now because of  that when i was using it and doing some  of those tasks it did not get that hot  on the bottom and the spot that it did  get the hottest was right at the center  that is right between your two feet if  it's on your lap so that is nice for  usability but the system does heat up to  108 degrees celsius in about 28  seconds which is way faster than the m1  model now the crazy thing is that there  is an empty large block of space that  would be perfect for a solid metal heat  spreader but instead it is just a gap of  air covered by the thin foil-like metal  which means that yes this was a  conscious decision to keep the chip  limited and with that the choice to have  a single nand for the ssd which makes it  dramatically slower if you care about  productivity now apple perfectly placed  this laptop in line to not make it too  good and too powerful like the m1  macbook air was and now we have a  perfect staircase of products that  guides you up the ladder to upgrade and  eventually reach the pro models because  of limitations that were placed there on  purpose which is what makes me sad this  machine is still excellent for most  people especially if you use the thermal  mod that costs 15 bucks doesn't void  your warranty it helps a ton  and it's gonna do a great job but once  you spec it up to this configuration and  especially if you upgrade the graphics  you are literally only a hundred dollars  away from buying the 14 inch at a  discount which is a much more capable  and nicer machine personally i've  greatly enjoyed using it it is so thin  it is so light and it just hurts me to  know that if we would have had a better  ssd at base and if we would have had a  heat spreader like on the m1  how much faster it would be  and for that price of the base model it  would have been a killer and then it  definitely would have still in sales  from that 14 inch now as far as the base  model  this thing is great for those that just  do email watching youtube videos maybe  editing one photo at a time and just  some very simple tasks and if that's  what you do and you don't need the extra  storage it will do the job great when i  started to do some productivity and  using it like i normally would i did  notice the slowdowns without doing any  benchmarking or trying to look for it  switching to the 16gb 512 model  it would just fly  wouldn't slow down for bursty tasks and  it would do a killer job so if you have  money if you can afford it and you want  the luxury in smaller size you will be  happy we are going to do more testing  we're going to find out if that 10 core  is worth that extra 100  uh we're gonna do some comparisons to a  windows laptop so make sure you guys  click above to subscribe to help us  reach our goal of a million subscribers  and for a chance to win comment down  below this has been max and i'll see you  in the next video  [Music]
 

